In Mobile Legends: Bang Bang (MLBB), the House of Paxley rules over Castle Aberleen, situated in the southern, misty reaches of the Moniyan Empire. As one of the empire's oldest, most prestigious, and secretly terrifying magic-wielding families—home to heroes like Aamon, Gusion, Valentina (their ancient ancestor), and Marcel (the soul photographer)—their estate is a structural masterpiece.To match their family motto, "Fear over love," the building balances high noble elegance with a dark, chilling undercurrent of forbidden magic.1. Architectural Style & Grand PersonaThe overall aesthetic of Castle Aberleen is a blend of Gothic Revival and Dark Baroque architecture, infused with floating magical elements. It is designed to look ancient, intimidating, and impeccably sharp.The Piercing SilhouetteThe estate does not feature flat, welcoming rooftops. Instead, it is dominated by razor-sharp, needle-like spires, flying buttresses, and jagged gargoyles that mimic the family's magical shards and blades. The rooftops are covered in deep slate-blue and dark violet tiles, which catch the faint sunlight.Materials and Color PaletteThe primary building material is a dark, reinforced granite block mixed with smooth obsidian. This stone gives the castle a matte-black and ash-gray finish. Strategically embedded through the masonry are veins of glowing magical light-ore and gold trims, striking a contrast between the family’s public allegiance to the Moniyan Empire's Light and their hidden practice of Dark Magic.2. Structural Composition & Exterior LayoutThe House of Paxley is a fortified palatial citadel rather than a simple home. It features a sprawling layout designed for privacy, defense, and magical experimentation.                  [ The Ancestral Spires ]
