                    [ The Iron Gates ]
The Mist-Enshrouded GatesThe entire estate is surrounded by iron gates forged into the shape of woven thorns. A perpetual, heavy magical fog wraps around the outer walls year-round. This is not natural weather; it is a defensive boundary that cloaks the estate from prying imperial eyes.The Obsidian CourtyardOnce past the gates, a massive courtyard made of polished black stone leads to the main entrance. In the center sits a towering, pristine marble statue of Valentina Paxley.3. Interior Aesthetics: The Upper Levels (The Public Face)Inside, the castle transitions from an intimidating fortress to a breathtakingly opulent noble estate. The upper floors are grand, symmetric, and rigidly organized.The Grand Mirror-Lined AtriumUpon entering, guests are met by soaring vaulted ceilings held up by pillars carved like armored knights.The Floors: Made of pristine, highly reflective white marble inlaid with gold geometric shapes.The Lighting: Massive crystal chandeliers hang from above, but instead of candles, they hold floating, enchanted shards of light magic that cast a cold, brilliant glow over the halls.The Left Wing: Aamon’s DomainAs the current Duke and head of the house, Aamon’s quarters and strategy rooms occupy the left wing.The Vibe: Everything here is sharp and immaculate. Cold silver filigree covers the walls, and the furniture is made of deep ebony wood.The Armory: Aamon's private chamber features glass display cases holding floating, shifting shards of invisible, light-bending glass and magical daggers.The Courtyard Academy & GroundsThis is where the younger Paxley siblings, including a rebellious teenage Gusion, were trained. It features grand indoor dueling arenas lined with enchanted glass that absorbs stray spellfire, and sprawling libraries containing thousands of tedious spellbooks and intricate magic scrolls.4. The Subterranean Levels (The Forbidden Shadows)Beneath the polished marble and glowing chandeliers lies the true heart of House Paxley—the lower levels, where the family's illicit dealings with dark magic and ancient entities take place.The Dark Magic Labs & Marcel’s StudioDeep below the castle, the pristine white marble gives way to rough-hewn stone walls lit by flickering, violet-hued torches.The Atmosphere: This area smells of ozone, cold iron, and old parchment.The Dark Chambers: This is where the enforcer Marcel operates, utilizing dark magic to trap souls within his camera lens. The rooms are cluttered with chemical baths for developing magical film, heavy iron chains, and dark altars dedicated to ancient prophecies.The Solitary VaultsA labyrinth of cold cells where the family "disciplined" rebellious members or hid those afflicted by the family's dark prophetic curses. These rooms are completely soundproofed and layered with heavy magical seals to prevent power leakages from being sensed by the Moniyan Monks.Summary of House Paxley's Visual DesignFeatureArchitectural ElementCultural / Magical SignificanceSpires & RoofsNeedle-sharp Gothic points, slate-blueEchoes Aamon and Gusion's affinity for blades.WindowsMassive stained-glass depicting ancient battlesFilters the outside mist into beautiful, eerie light.Main AtriumWhite marble, floating gold shardsThe public "Noble Face" presented to the Moniyan Empire.UndergroundObsidian blocks, violet flames, hidden labsThe true "Shadow Face" where forbidden magic is cast.